  "question": {
    "text": "In a photoelectric effect measurement, the stopping potential for a given metal is found to be <math><msub><mrow><mi>V</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>0</mn></mrow></msub></math> volt when radiation of wavelength <math><msub><mrow><mi>λ</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>0</mn></mrow></msub></math> is used. If radiation of wavelength <math><msub><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi>λ</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>0</mn></mrow></msub></math> is used with the same metal then the stopping potential (in volt) will be",
    "image": null
  },
